{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Burned</b> — In feminine language, like פורת. And see the verse above: 'it is also כה,' and likewise וראה. Understand: this one is burned with fire, swept away and prepared, and understand that both are destroyed by the rebuke of Your face — the opposite of 'shine Your face.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is textually difficult throughout. פורת, כה, וראה, והכנה, and 'swept away and prepared' (סוחה והכנה) may be corrupt or abbreviated cross-references; rendered hyper-literally without resolution. The final clause alludes to the priestly blessing (Numbers 6:25), opposite of destruction."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:36.804540780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}